    scenario: "? vs ? — üõ°Ô∏èThe Slav Defenseüõ°Ô∏è: Modern Slav‚ö° — Move 4. Bg2 — FEN: rn1qkb1r/pp3ppp/2p1pn2/5b2/2QP4/5NP1/PP2PP1P/RNB1KB1R w KQkq - 0 4",
    idealResponse: `This is the Modern Slav, very tricky. It is not great, but if you play against an opponent who is not ready you have better chances of winning. Your plans are Nbd2, Be7 followed by 0-0, and Qc7 finnishing development and connecting the rooks and bringing them into the center. In the middlgame, try going for the break e5. You have a nice Caro-Kann structure, very solid :D [%csl Rg2,Bd7,Be7,Bg8,Ye5,Bc7][%cal Rf1g2,Bb8d7,Bf8e7,Be8g8,Ye6e5,Bd8c7]`,
