    idealResponse: `Surprisingly common amongst beginner and intermediate players. When starting out, players are taught the Italian Game (e4 e5 Nf3 Nc6 Bc4) which is a great opening to learn piece development and center control. But these moves are not automatic. I'll be blunt, but against the Kan, it is just plain bad. The a2-g8 diagonal is already closed, so the bishop is not going places on c4. To make matters worse, d5 comes with tempo!`,
